# Copy to .env.local for local development (`npm run dev`), and add the same
# variables in Cloudflare → Workers & Pages → thediadem → Settings → Variables and Secrets
# (type: Secret, for both Production and Preview).

# --- Server only (used by functions/api/contact.ts and functions/api/assistant.ts). Never prefix these with VITE_. ---
# GoHighLevel → Settings → Private Integrations → token with
# "View Contacts" and "Edit Contacts" scopes
GHL_API_TOKEN=
# Sub-account (location) ID, from the GoHighLevel URL: /v2/location/<ID>/...
GHL_LOCATION_ID=8WJ6nyFWjFzTgnujES0n
# Optional: extra comma-separated tags added to every website lead
# GHL_TAGS=website-lead
# Optional: calendar that discovery calls are booked on (Calendars → Calendar settings →
# the calendar's ID). The contact form then only offers times that are free on it and
# books the chosen time, and the "Crest" chat books on it too. The token also needs the
# "View Calendars" and "Edit Calendar Events" scopes. Without it, the chosen date/time is
# only noted on the contact, and Crest saves a request for the team to confirm.
# GHL_CALENDAR_ID=
# The website chat runs on GHL Conversations (Kiara answers there; functions/_lib/liveChat.ts).
# The token then also needs "View/Edit Conversations" and "View/Edit Conversation Messages".
#
# "Website chat" reply channel, from the "Diadem Website Chat" Marketplace app
# (marketplace.gohighlevel.com → My Apps; redirect URL https://www.thediadem.ca/api/chat-connect,
# conversation provider delivery URL https://www.thediadem.ca/api/live-webhook). With all
# three set, the GHL_TOKENS KV binding (wrangler.jsonc) and the app installed on The Diadem,
# the team replies on "Website chat" and replies appear only in the chat. Without them, they
# reply by email or SMS, which also reaches the visitor's inbox or phone.
# GHL_CONVERSATION_PROVIDER_ID=
# GHL_CLIENT_ID=
# GHL_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- Server only (used by functions/api/assistant.ts, the "Crest" chat). Never prefix with VITE_. ---
# Anthropic API key: the assistant answers with Claude. It books consultations with the GHL_* values above.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Optional: override the Claude model (default: claude-opus-5-5)
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=

# --- Browser (optional) ---
# Override where the contact form posts. Defaults to /api/contact.
# VITE_CONTACT_ENDPOINT=
# Optional: override where the assistant posts. Defaults to /api/assistant (Claude).
# If that fails, it answers from the FAQs and services already on the site.
# VITE_ASSISTANT_ENDPOINT=
